        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0283" n="1243" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1243"/>

                <head>No. 823.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Whitehouse to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 16, 1888</date>.
                        (Received November 24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 188.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer you to my
                    dispatch No. 182, of the 12th instant, in reply to your telegram of the 10th,
                    asking that a formal request for the extradition of Shields and Wilson be made
                    of the Mexican Government.</p>
                <p>I spoke with Señor Mariscal concerning his promise to telegraph the governor of
                    Coahuila about the matter, and he read me a telegram, in which the governor
                    states that no request for extradition has been made to him.</p>
                <p>I therefore sent you yesterday a telegram to that effect.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Remsen
                    Whitehouse.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d110-a1.xml" xpointer="d110-a1"/>
            </div>
